          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#AsASloganForTheRyuTakayanagiFormula"} As a slogan for the Ryu-Takayanagi formula
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_entries"} Related entries
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The symbols
            %em ER = EPR
            (pronounced: “ee arr is ee pee arr”) serve as a slogan for a hypothesis about
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entangled+particles"} entangled particles
            (the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/EPR+paradox"} Einstein-Podolsky-Rosen phenomenon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wormhole"} wormhole
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Rosen+bridge"}> Einstein-Rosen bridge
            \: “ER”).
          %p
            This slogan is due to
            %a{:href => "#MaldacenaSusskind13"} Maldacena &amp; Susskind (2013)
            (there motivated from a search for a solution for the perceived
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole+firewall+problem"} black hole firewall problem
            = succeed "&rbrack;." do
              %a{:href => "#VerlindeVerlinde22"} Verlinde &amp; Verlinde (2022)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ryu-Takayanagi+formula"} Ryu-Takayanagi formula
            %a{:href => "#AsASloganForTheRyuTakayanagiFormula"} below
            (which, however, applies in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic
            context, a qualification not necessarily brought out by
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#MaldacenaSusskind13"} Maldacena &amp; Susskind
          %p
            At face value the statement “ER = EPR”, even if parsed benevolently, suffers from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+checking"} typing error
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://twitter.com/schreiberurs/status/1134503200550203392?lang=en"} like with a Zen koan
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paradox"} paradoxical
            formulation to propel the intuitive grasp of indeed rather deep principles of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holography
            and particularly of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+entanglement+entropy"} holographic entanglement entropy
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AsASloganForTheRyuTakayanagiFormula"} Ryu-Takayanagi formula
          %p
            Another source of fun with the slogan “ER = EPR” is to thereby see the two classical and seminal papers by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Einstein"} Albert Einstein
            et al. from 1935 &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "wormhole#EinsteinRosen35"}> Einstein &amp; Rosen (1935)
            ,
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "EPR+paradox#EinsteinPodoldskyRosen35"} Einstein, Podoldsky &amp; Rosen (1935)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein"} Einstein
            must have seemed unrelated — to secretly be about two sides of the same medal.
          %h2#AsASloganForTheRyuTakayanagiFormula As a slogan for the Ryu-Takayanagi formula
          %p
            The idea meant to be expressed by the slogan “ER = EPR” may usefully be compared to – and may be a way of turning into prose – the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ryu-Takayanagi+formula"} Ryu-Takayanagi formula
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#RyuTakayanagi06a"}> Ryu &amp; Takayanagi (2006)
            \&amp;rbrack; (which has a more well-defined content as a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theorem"} theorem
            in a class of discrete
            = succeed "-models)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
          %ul
            %li
              %strong (quantum entanglement:)
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
              in a subspace of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
          %p with
          %ul
            %li
              %strong (global spacetime structure:)
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+surface"} minimal area
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coboundary"} cobounding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypersurface"} hypersurface
              in an ambient
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curved
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          %p
            Concretely, in
            = succeed "-models" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS2%2FCFT1+duality"} AdS2/CFT1 duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_A
            of any
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+dimer+code"} Majorana dimer code
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} state
            turns out to count the number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimers"} dimers
            that cross between a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"}> connected
            ) subregion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
