          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/HanUniversalHolographicCode.jpg", :width => "380px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "holographic+entanglement+entropy#Yan20"} Yan 20
          %p
            In the case that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimers"} dimers
            correspond to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+tesselation"} hyperbolic tesselation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 5
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{5,4\}
            from the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HaPPY+code"} HaPPY code
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mi ln
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi Chords
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo |
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_A
                  \\;=\;
                  \\tfrac{1}{2}
                  \\ln
                  \\big(
                  2^{ \left\vert Chords(A, \bar A) \right\vert }
                  \\big)
          %p
            recovers the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ryu-Takayanagi+formula"} Ryu-Takayanagi formula
            (
            %a{:href => "holographic+entanglement+entropy#JGPE19"}> JGPE 19 (78)
            ), as here the number of chords crossing any hyperbolic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic"} geodesic
            grows linearly with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/length"} length
            of this geodesic.
          %p
            A precursor to this picture is the “bit-thread”-interpretation of entanglement entropy due to
            %a{:href => "holographic+entanglement+entropy#FreedmanHeadrick16"} Freedman &amp; Headrick 16
            (notice the use of “EPR pair” in their
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1604.00354.pdf#page=4"} Figure 4
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/ChordDiagram.jpg", :width => "230px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber19c"} Sati  Schreiber 19c
          %p
            Following
            %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber19c"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
            we recognize the above
            = succeed "/bit-thread" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+dimer"} Majorana dimer
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#JGPE19"} JGPE 19
            %a{:href => "#Yan19"} Yan 19
            as
            = succeed "-encodings" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagram"} chord diagram
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.10425v3.pdf#page=38"} p. 38
          %p
            Notice that the formula for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+dimer+code"} Majorana dimer code
            holds generally, for
            %em any
            configuration and hence any underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagram"} chord diagram
          %p
            In conclusion, note how each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord"} chord
            here reflects at the same time:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                (ER) one
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement"} entangled pair
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbits"} qbits
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum system
            %li
              %p
                (EPR) a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic"} geodesic
                through the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+plane"} hyperbolic plane
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
                spacetime,
          %p which is a (rigorous) state of affairs clearly reminiscent of the “ER = EPR” slogan (except that wormholes are replaced by minimal area hypersurfaces, here: geodesics).
          %p
            For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+entanglement+entropy"} holographic entanglement entropy
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement"}> entanglement
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/EPR+paradox"} EPR paradox
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wormhole"} wormhole
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+entanglement+entropy"} holographic entanglement entropy
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+teleportation"} quantum teleportation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole+firewall+problem"} black hole firewall problem
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The original result of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ryu-Takayanagi+formula"} Ryu-Takayanagi formula
          %ul
            %li#RyuTakayanagi06a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shinsei+Ryu"}> Shinsei Ryu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadashi+Takayanagi"} Tadashi Takayanagi
              = succeed "," do
                %em Holographic Derivation of Entanglement Entropy from AdS/CFT
              %strong 96
              181602 (2006) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0603001"}> arXiv:hep-th/0603001
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.96.181602"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.96.181602
          %p The slogan “ER = EPR” is due to:
          %ul
            %li#MaldacenaSusskind13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Maldacena"}> Juan Maldacena
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cool horizons for entangled black holes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.0533"} arXiv:1306.0533
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/prop.201300020"} doi:10.1002/prop.201300020
            %li#Susskind14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"}> Leonard Susskind
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em ER=EPR, GHZ, and the consistency of quantum measurements
                %strong 64
                1 (2016) 72-83 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.8483"}> arXiv:1412.8483
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/prop.201500094"} doi:10.1002/prop.201500094
          %p An email exchange of similar content that happened half a year earlier is recalled in:
          %ul
            %li#VerlindeVerlinde22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Verlinde"}> Erik Verlinde
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herman+Verlinde"} Herman Verlinde
              %em A Conversation on ER = EPR
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.09389"}> arXiv:2212.09389
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ER%3DEPR"} ER=EPR
            %li
              %p
                Xin Jiang, Peng Wang, Houwen Wu, Haitang Yang:
                %em Realization of “ER=EPR”
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.18485"}> arXiv:2411.18485
                \&amp;rbrack;
